---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../lib/site";
import { localizePath , pick } from "../../i18n/utils";

const lang = (Astro.currentLocale ?? "en") as "en" | "zh";

const slug = "tailscale-ssh-setup";

const C = pick({
  en: {
    heading: "Connect with Tailscale SSH",
    intro:
      "Reach machines on your tailnet by their MagicDNS name from VVTerm — no port forwarding, no exposed ports, and no extra SSH keys to manage.",
    meta: "Guide",
    title: "Connect with Tailscale SSH — VVTerm",
    description:
      "Enable Tailscale SSH on your host with tailscale up --ssh, set ACLs, and connect to the MagicDNS name from VVTerm — no port forwarding or exposed ports.",
    schemaDescription:
      "Step-by-step guide to using Tailscale SSH with VVTerm: install Tailscale on the host and device, enable SSH, set ACLs, and connect to a MagicDNS name with no port forwarding.",
    bodyHtml: `
  <p>
    Tailscale puts your devices on a private mesh network and can handle SSH authentication for you with <strong>Tailscale SSH</strong>. With it, you reach a server by its tailnet name from VVTerm — no public
    ports, no port forwarding, and no separate SSH keys to distribute.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    Every machine you join to your tailnet gets a stable private address and a <strong>MagicDNS</strong> name like <code>myserver.tailnet-name.ts.net</code>. When Tailscale SSH is enabled, Tailscale itself
    authenticates connections between devices in your tailnet based on your access policy, so the server
    never needs an inbound port open to the public internet.
  </p>

  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>A <strong>Tailscale account</strong> with the host and your iPhone, iPad, or Mac both joined to the same tailnet.</li>
    <li><strong>Tailscale installed on the host</strong> you want to reach.</li>
    <li>Tailscale running on the <strong>device</strong> you're connecting from, signed into the same account.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Enable Tailscale SSH on the host</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      On the server, bring Tailscale up with the SSH flag:
      <pre><code>sudo tailscale up --ssh</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>This advertises the host as accepting Tailscale SSH connections. Authentication is handled by Tailscale rather than by traditional SSH keys.</li>
    <li>
      Confirm the host's tailnet name and status:
      <pre><code>tailscale status</code></pre>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Allow SSH in your ACLs</h2>
  <p>
    Tailscale SSH access is governed by the <strong>SSH rules</strong> in your tailnet's access control
    policy. In the Tailscale admin console, make sure your policy includes an <code>ssh</code> section that
    permits your user to reach the host as the desired login user. Without a matching rule, the connection
    is refused even though the host is online. Save the policy before you connect.
  </p>

  <h2>Connect from VVTerm</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>In VVTerm, tap <strong>Add Server</strong> (or edit an existing server).</li>
    <li>Set the <strong>host</strong> to the machine's <strong>MagicDNS name</strong>, for example <code>myserver.tailnet-name.ts.net</code>. You can also use its tailnet IP address.</li>
    <li>Keep the port at <code>22</code> and enter the <strong>username</strong> you want to log in as on the host.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Tailscale SSH</strong> as the connection method so authentication is handled through your tailnet.</li>
    <li>Save and tap the server to connect.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>No port forwarding required</h2>
  <p>
    Because traffic rides the encrypted tailnet, you do <strong>not</strong> open port 22 to the internet,
    configure a router, or punch holes in a firewall. The host can sit behind NAT or a strict firewall and
    still be reachable from your devices, anywhere they have a connection.
  </p>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>If the name doesn't resolve, confirm MagicDNS is enabled for your tailnet and that the host shows as connected in <code>tailscale status</code>.</li>
    <li>If you connect but get permission denied, revisit your ACL <code>ssh</code> rules and the login user you requested.</li>
    <li>If the device can't see the host at all, make sure both are signed into the same Tailscale account and online.</li>
  </ul>
`,
  },
  zh: {
    heading: "使用 Tailscale SSH 连接",
    intro:
      "在 VVTerm 中通过 MagicDNS 名称连接 tailnet 中的机器 —— 无需端口转发、无需暴露端口，也无需额外管理 SSH 密钥。",
    meta: "指南",
    title: "使用 Tailscale SSH 连接 — VVTerm",
    description:
      "用 tailscale up --ssh 在主机上启用 Tailscale SSH、设置 ACL，并从 VVTerm 连接 MagicDNS 名称 —— 无需端口转发或暴露端口。",
    schemaDescription:
      "在 VVTerm 中使用 Tailscale SSH 的分步指南：在主机和设备上安装 Tailscale、启用 SSH、设置 ACL，并连接 MagicDNS 名称，无需端口转发。",
    bodyHtml: `
  <p>
    Tailscale 把你的设备置于一个私有网状网络中，并能通过 <strong>Tailscale SSH</strong> 为你处理 SSH 认证。借助它，你可以在 VVTerm 中通过 tailnet 名称连接服务器 —— 无需公网端口、无需端口转发，也无需分发单独的 SSH 密钥。
  </p>

  <h2>工作原理</h2>
  <p>
    你加入 tailnet 的每一台机器都会获得一个稳定的私有地址和一个像 <code>myserver.tailnet-name.ts.net</code> 这样的 <strong>MagicDNS</strong> 名称。启用 Tailscale SSH 后，Tailscale 本身会根据你的访问策略对 tailnet 内设备之间的连接进行认证，因此服务器无需向公网开放任何入站端口。
  </p>

  <h2>前置条件</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>一个 <strong>Tailscale 账户</strong>，且主机与你的 iPhone、iPad 或 Mac 都加入了同一个 tailnet。</li>
    <li>在你要连接的<strong>主机上安装了 Tailscale</strong>。</li>
    <li>你用来连接的<strong>设备</strong>上运行着 Tailscale，并登录了同一个账户。</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>在主机上启用 Tailscale SSH</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      在服务器上，带 SSH 标志启动 Tailscale：
      <pre><code>sudo tailscale up --ssh</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>这会将主机声明为接受 Tailscale SSH 连接。认证由 Tailscale 处理，而非传统的 SSH 密钥。</li>
    <li>
      确认主机的 tailnet 名称和状态：
      <pre><code>tailscale status</code></pre>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>在 ACL 中允许 SSH</h2>
  <p>
    Tailscale SSH 访问由你 tailnet 访问控制策略中的 <strong>SSH 规则</strong>管理。在 Tailscale 管理控制台中，确保你的策略包含一个 <code>ssh</code> 段，允许你的用户以期望的登录用户身份连接主机。若没有匹配的规则，即使主机在线，连接也会被拒绝。连接前请保存策略。
  </p>

  <h2>从 VVTerm 连接</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>在 VVTerm 中点按 <strong>Add Server</strong>（或编辑现有服务器）。</li>
    <li>将<strong>主机</strong>设为机器的 <strong>MagicDNS 名称</strong>，例如 <code>myserver.tailnet-name.ts.net</code>。你也可以使用它的 tailnet IP 地址。</li>
    <li>端口保持 <code>22</code>，并输入你想在主机上登录的<strong>用户名</strong>。</li>
    <li>选择 <strong>Tailscale SSH</strong> 作为连接方式，以便通过你的 tailnet 处理认证。</li>
    <li>保存并点按服务器进行连接。</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>无需端口转发</h2>
  <p>
    由于流量行经加密的 tailnet，你<strong>无需</strong>向互联网开放 22 端口、配置路由器或在防火墙上打洞。主机可以位于 NAT 或严格防火墙之后，仍能从你的设备在任何有网络的地方访问。
  </p>

  <h2>故障排查</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>如果名称无法解析，请确认你的 tailnet 已启用 MagicDNS，且主机在 <code>tailscale status</code> 中显示为已连接。</li>
    <li>如果连接成功但提示权限被拒，请重新检查你的 ACL <code>ssh</code> 规则以及你请求的登录用户。</li>
    <li>如果设备完全看不到主机，请确保两者都登录了同一个 Tailscale 账户并处于在线状态。</li>
  </ul>
`,
  },
}, lang);

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  name: C.heading,
  description: C.schemaDescription,
  url: `${SITE.siteUrl}${localizePath(`/guides/${slug}`, lang)}`,
};
---

<DocsLayout
  kind="guides"
  activeSlug={slug}
  heading={C.heading}
  intro={C.intro}
  meta={C.meta}
  title={C.title}
  description={C.description}
  canonicalPath={`/guides/${slug}`}
  structuredData={[articleSchema]}
>
  <Fragment set:html={C.bodyHtml} />
</DocsLayout>
